WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.230
Three women.

2
00:00:01.280 --> 00:00:02.790
Three rooms.

3
00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:07.090
A bedchamber, a castle
corridor, a street at night.

4
00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.950
Beside each, a hand pins up a card.

5
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.100
A different hand each time.

6
00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:16.310
In the street, one of them
answers back: "I am no strumpet,

7
00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:20.000
but of life as honest as
you that thus abuse me."

8
00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:22.520
So who writes these labels?

9
00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:25.140
In this mission, you'll
meet a senator's daughter,

10
00:00:25.190 --> 00:00:29.200
her attendant, and a woman
in Cyprus whom Cassio visits.

11
00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:34.180
You'll see what marriage meant in 1604,
when a wife's legal identity was covered

12
00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:35.600
by her husband's.

13
00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:38.700
And you'll weigh critics who
read the play through gender,

14
00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:41.790
from 1817 to 1996.

15
00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:45.040
Your mission: find out who gets to say so.
